{"term":"prospect","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:cf6638818eca37d5c3","definition":"The region which the eye overlooks at one time; a view; a scene; an outlook.","example":"As when a Scout[…]Obtains the brow of ſome high-climbing Hill, / Which to his eye diſcovers unaware / The goodly proſpect of ſome forein land / Firſt-ſeen, or ſome renownd Metropolis / With gliſtering Spires and Pinnacles adornd, / Which now the Riſing Sun guilds with his beams.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["Mount Prospect","nonprospect","prospectless","Prospect Vale","unqualified prospect"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prospect#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:536a5a061e09877748","definition":"A picturesque or panoramic view; a landscape; hence, a sketch of a landscape.","example":"I went to Putney, and other places on the Thames, to take prospects in crayon, to carry into France, where I thought to have them engraved.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["Mount Prospect","nonprospect","prospectless","Prospect Vale","unqualified prospect"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prospect#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e00f7fbad5caaca55c","definition":"A position affording a fine view; a lookout.","example":"Him God beholding from his proſpect high, / Wherein paſt, preſent, future he beholds, / Thus to his onely Son forſeeing ſpake.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["Mount Prospect","nonprospect","prospectless","Prospect Vale","unqualified prospect"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prospect#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8d25b6128ad83ba4d6","definition":"A relative position of the front of a building or other structure; a face; a relative aspect.","example":"Their prospect was toward the south.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["Mount Prospect","nonprospect","prospectless","Prospect Vale","unqualified prospect"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prospect#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e51e8927eb843ef046","definition":"The act of looking forward; foresight; anticipation.","example":"a very ill prospect of a future state","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["Mount Prospect","nonprospect","prospectless","Prospect Vale","unqualified prospect"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prospect#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:076244bc04d816b0d8","definition":"The potential things that may come to pass, often favorable.","example":"The result, therefore, of this physical inquiry is, that we find no vestige of a beginning,— no prospect of an end.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["outcome"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["Mount Prospect","nonprospect","prospectless","Prospect Vale","unqualified prospect"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prospect#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2a97d3a3bbc7c0fada","definition":"A hope; a hopeful.","example":"The most persistent tormentor was Alex Oxlade-Chamberlain, who scored a hat-trick in last month’s corresponding fixture in Iceland. His ability to run at defences is instantly striking, but it is his clever use of possession that has persuaded some shrewd judges that he is an even better prospect than Theo Walcott.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["Mount Prospect","nonprospect","prospectless","Prospect Vale","unqualified prospect"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prospect#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:781ac890e40c2569d2","definition":"Any player whose rights are owned by a top-level professional team, but who has yet to play a game for said team.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["Mount Prospect","nonprospect","prospectless","Prospect Vale","unqualified prospect"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prospect#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d87705d0bd86e15c1d","definition":"A potential client or customer.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["Mount Prospect","nonprospect","prospectless","Prospect Vale","unqualified prospect"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prospect#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:bd70558e6b782fa1ed","definition":"The façade of an organ.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["Mount Prospect","nonprospect","prospectless","Prospect Vale","unqualified prospect"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prospect#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:659804e1eab78e9bf3","definition":"To search, as for gold.","example":"Among the ancient sites in the Taklamakan Desert which are frequented by Khotan \"treasure seekers,\" and which the prospecting parties sent out by me had visited, none seemed to offer better opportunities for systematic excavations than the one known to them as Dandan-Uilik.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["Mount Prospect","nonprospect","prospectless","Prospect Vale","unqualified prospect","bioprospect","prospector","unprospected"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prospect#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:cf049af58de28e6b40","definition":"To determine which minerals or metals are present in a location.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["Mount Prospect","nonprospect","prospectless","Prospect Vale","unqualified prospect","bioprospect","prospector","unprospected"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prospect#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c2d12ec670c46dfbea","definition":"To have or afford a view; to face or look out.","example":"This poynte ſemethe as though it woolde inuade the monte Atlas in Aphrica. Foꝛ it pꝛoſpectethe [translating spectat] towarde that parte of Aphꝛike, whiche the poꝛtugales caule Caput Bonæ Sperantiæ.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"intransitive, obsolete","wordFamily":["Mount Prospect","nonprospect","prospectless","Prospect Vale","unqualified prospect","bioprospect","prospector","unprospected"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prospect#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6a0896f46b735906aa","definition":"To look or face towards; to view.","example":"Beynge therfoꝛe ioyfull and gladde of the frendeſhyppe of owre men, he tooke the capitaine by the hand and bꝛought him with certeine of his familiars to the higheſt towre of his palaice, from whenſe they myght proſpecte [translating dispectare] the mayne ſea.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete, transitive","wordFamily":["Mount Prospect","nonprospect","prospectless","Prospect Vale","unqualified prospect","bioprospect","prospector","unprospected"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prospect#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:12d629a6f60a224756","definition":"A number of places in the United States:","example":"","pos":"name","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["Mount Prospect","nonprospect","prospectless","Prospect Vale","unqualified prospect","bioprospect","prospector","unprospected"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Prospect#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e9187be7b24a88553c","definition":"A suburb of Sydney, New South Wales, Australia.","example":"","pos":"name","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["Mount Prospect","nonprospect","prospectless","Prospect Vale","unqualified prospect","bioprospect","prospector","unprospected"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Prospect#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:44e6b86d6df8ba73cf","definition":"An inner suburb of Adelaide, South Australia.","example":"","pos":"name","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usag